A method provider on a generic alias to an anonymous interface instantiates by
demand: the *Box[int] consumer pins T=int, and the method binds to a value of the
instantiated alias (source.Fetch()). The owner is carried as a *types.Alias
throughout, not a defined type.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Box[T any] struct{ V T }

type Source[T any] = interface {
	//plumb:build
	Fetch() *Box[T]
}

//plumb:build
func mkSource() Source[int] { return nil }

//plumb:build
func use(p *Box[int]) string { return "" }
